 "thread": "iMpOa7N_TmE",
 "subject": "How to \"find\" in console output?",
 "messages_listed": 5,
 "last_activity": "2015-07-18T00:40:56Z",
 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "zH2ZDQKz3_gJ",
   "from": "Michael",
   "author": "6e4e37c602c2b104",
   "date": "2015-07-17T23:28:14Z",
   "subject": "How to \"find\" in console output?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Stupid question perhaps, but I need to do ctrl-F style finding in my console output. I&#39;m on Windows. Don&#39;t see a way to do it in RStudio or the R GUI. Can do it in my console emulator, but as I&#39;m set up now, that&#39;s inconvenient because I have to paste back and forth from the script. So two possible solutions: is there some kind of ctrl-F functionality for output in RStudio or the R GUI, or is there a convenient way to send lines from a script file to my console emulator (cmder), like ctrl-Enter in RStudio?</div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "i8o3wbFH8n8J",
   "from": "Noam Ross",
   "author": "8c8f0ca54c4a2459",
   "date": "2015-07-17T23:55:42Z",
   "subject": "Re: [D-RUG]: How to \"find\" in console output?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"font-size:13px;font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,arial,freesans,clean,sans-serif;color:rgb(34,34,34);border:none;line-height:20px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><p style=\"margin:1em 0px\">This may not quite cover your needs, but <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:nowrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">sink(&quot;output.txt&quot;, split=TRUE)</code> will send your console output to <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:nowrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">output.txt</code> as well as the console window.  From there you can search the file however you please.  <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:nowrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">sink(&quot;output.txt&quot;, type=&quot;message&quot;)</code> will record messages (Errors and warnings, mostly), but for some reason doesn’t allow <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:nowrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">split=TRUE</code>, so you don’t see them in your console.  <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:nowrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">sink(NULL)</code> when you’re done stops recording the output.</p>\r\n<div title=\"MDH:VGhpcyBtYXkgbm90IHF1aXRlIGNvdmVyIHl