   "subject": "Re: [D-RUG]: How to \"find\" in console output?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div>Sorry. Now that I actually read your full question, I see you&#39;ve got that going. <br><br></div>Both emacs (ESS) and vim (using some tmux thing -- see Vince&#39;s page here <a href=\"https://github.com/vsbuffalo/devnotes/wiki/Vim,-R,-and-Tmux:-Minimal-Configuration\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/vsbuffalo/devnotes/wiki/Vim,-R,-and-Tmux:-Minimal-Configuration&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792467981550000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1irfvIy3nvh1niGR07hs7P\">https://github.com/vsbuffalo/devnotes/wiki/Vim,-R,-and-Tmux:-Minimal-Configuration</a> ) can send lines from a script file to terminal.<br><br></div>sinking and searching is probably the way to go<br></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Fri, Jul 17, 2015 at 5:38 PM, Jaime Ashander <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">jash...@ucdavis.edu</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Using R in a bash-similar shell (e.g. on standard shell on mac os x or unix, or cygwin on windows), CTRL-r will do a &#39;reverse-i-search&#39;. Start typing the search and the first match will show up, hit CTRL-r for subsequent matches<br></div><div><div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Fri, Jul 17, 2015 at 5:10 PM, Michael Levy <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">mle...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif;font-size:small\">Thanks. That is definitely an improvement.</div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><span><font color=\"#888888\"><br clear=\"all\"><div><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><p><font face=\"tahoma, sans-serif\" size=\"1\"><i>-- <br></i></font><i style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif;font-size:x-small\">Michael Levy<br></i><i style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif;font-size:x-small\">c: <a href=\"tel:304-376-4523\" value=\"+13043764523\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">304-376-4523</a></i></p></div></div></div></font></span><div><div>\r\n<br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Fri, Jul 17, 2015 at 4:55 PM, Noam Ross <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">noam...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"font-size:13px;font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,arial,freesans,clean,sans-serif;color:rgb(34,34,34);border:none;line-heig